an4.28:7.1 starts: Who can obstruct the dispeller
an4.28:7.2 starts: who has discarded all kamma?
an4.28:7.3 starts: Who is fit to blame one who is
an4.28:7.4 starts: a coin of refined gold?
an4.28:7.5 starts: Even the devas praise such a one;
an4.28:7.6 starts: by Brahmā too he is praised.
an4.33:3.1 starts: When, through direct knowledge,
an4.33:3.2 starts: the Buddha, the teacher, the peerless person
an4.33:3.3 starts: in this world with its devas,
an4.33:3.4 starts: sets in motion the wheel of Dhamma,
an4.34:5.1 starts: For those confident in regard to the foremost,
an4.34:5.2 starts: knowing the foremost Dhamma,
an4.34:5.3 starts: confident in the Buddha—the foremost—
an4.34:5.4 starts: unsurpassed, worthy of offerings;
an4.35:6.1 starts: He who found for the sake of all
an4.35:6.2 starts: release from the snare of death;
an4.35:6.3 starts: who revealed the Dhamma, the method,
an4.35:6.4 starts: for the benefit of devas and humans;
an4.35:6.5 starts: he in whom many people gain confidence
an4.35:6.6 starts: when they see and listen to him;
an4.36:5.1 starts: “I have destroyed those taints by which
an4.36:5.2 starts: I might have been reborn as a deva
an4.36:5.3 starts: or as a gandhabba that travels through the
an4.36:5.4 starts: by which I might have reached the state
an4.36:5.5 starts: or arrived back at the human state:
an4.36:5.6 starts: I have dispelled and cut down these taints.
an4.39:3.1 starts: The horse sacrifice, human sacrifice,
an4.39:3.2 starts: sammāpāsa, vājapeyya, niraggaḷa:
an4.39:3.3 starts: these grand sacrifices, fraught with violence,
an4.39:3.4 starts: do not bring great fruit.
an4.39:5.1 starts: But when they regularly offer by family custom
an4.39:5.2 starts: sacrifices free from violence,
an4.39:5.3 starts: no goats, sheep, and cattle
an4.39:5.4 starts: or various creatures are slain.
an4.39:5.5 starts: That is the sacrifice the great seers
an4.39:5.6 starts: of right conduct attend.
an4.3:5.1 starts: For a hundred thousand and thirty-six
an4.3:5.2 starts: nirabbudas, plus five abbudas,
an4.3:5.3 starts: the slanderer of noble ones goes to hell,
an4.3:5.4 starts: having defamed them with evil speech and mind.
an4.40:3.1 starts: When a sacrifice is timely and allowable,
an4.40:3.2 starts: well prepared and nonviolent,
an4.40:3.3 starts: the self-controlled followers of the spiritual life
an4.40:3.4 starts: attend such a sacrifice as this.
an4.40:4.1 starts: Those in the world who have removed the
an4.40:4.2 starts: transcenders of time and destination,
an4.40:4.3 starts: the Buddhas who are proficient in sacrifice,
an4.40:4.4 starts: praise this kind of sacrifice.
an4.51:7.1 starts: Just as the many rivers used by the
an4.51:7.2 starts: flowing downstream, reach the ocean,
an4.51:7.3 starts: the great mass of water, the boundless sea,
an4.51:7.4 starts: the fearsome receptacle of heaps of gems;
an4.51:8.1 starts: so the streams of merit reach the wise
an4.51:8.2 starts: who is a giver of food, drink, and
an4.51:8.3 starts: they reach the donor of beds, seats, and
an4.51:8.4 starts: like rivers carrying their waters to the sea.
an4.52:7.1 starts: Therefore an intelligent person,
an4.52:7.2 starts: remembering the Buddhas’ teaching,
an4.52:7.3 starts: should be intent on faith and virtuous behavior,
an4.52:7.4 starts: confidence and vision of the Dhamma.
an4.55:4.1 starts: Both husband and wife are endowed with faith,
an4.55:4.2 starts: charitable and self-controlled,
an4.55:4.3 starts: living their lives righteously,
an4.55:4.4 starts: addressing each other with pleasant words,
